   "id": "taanit.28a.15",
   "daf": "28a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "בְּאֶחָד בְּטֵבֵת שָׁבוּ בְּנֵי פַרְעוֹשׁ שְׁנִיָּה כּוּ׳. מַנִּי מַתְנִיתִין? לָא רַבִּי מֵאִיר, וְלָא רַבִּי יְהוּדָה, וְלָא רַבִּי יוֹסֵי. אִי רַבִּי מֵאִיר, לִיתְנֵי: שָׁבוּ בְּנֵי דָוִד בֶּן יְהוּדָה שְׁנִיָּה!",
   "en": "The mishna taught: «On the first of Tevet, the descendants of Parosh returned» to bring wood for «a second» time. The Gemara asks: «Who is» the author of this opinion of «the mishna?» It is «not» the opinion of «Rabbi Meir, nor» that of «Rabbi Yehuda, nor» that of «Rabbi Yosei.» The Gemara elaborates: «If it» represents the opinion of «Rabbi Meir, let him teach,» with regard to the twentieth of Av, that «the descendants of David ben Yehuda returned» for «a second» time. According to Rabbi Meir, the descendants of Pahath Moab are the descendants of David, and consequently they would return for a second time on that date."
  }
 ],
